==Notes==
* The first word also increases the damage of unarmed power attacks.
* Not mentioned in the description for the third tier shout is that several shouts have their magnitudes and/or durations amplified. In general, shouts with point values (i.e. [[Skyrim:Frost Breath|Frost Breath]]) are enhanced by 25%, while shouts with duration are enhanced by 50%. The one exception to this rule is [[Skyrim:Ice Form|Ice Form]], which is increased in duration by 25%.
** Shouts which have neither magnitude nor duration affected: 
***Shouts introduced with the Dawnguard or Dragonborn DLC ([[Skyrim:Battle Fury|Battle Fury]], [[Skyrim:Bend Will|Bend Will]], [[Skyrim:Cyclone|Cyclone]], [[Skyrim:Drain Vitality|Drain Vitality]], [[Skyrim:Soul Tear|Soul Tear]], and [[Skyrim:Summon Durnehviir|Summon Durnehviir]])
***[[Skyrim:Call Dragon|Call Dragon]], [[Skyrim:Clear Skies|Clear Skies]], [[Skyrim:Dragonrend|Dragonrend]], [[Skyrim:Storm Call|Storm Call]], [[Skyrim:Throw Voice|Throw Voice]], [[Skyrim:Unrelenting Force|Unrelenting Force]], and [[Skyrim:Whirlwind Sprint|Whirlwind Sprint]]
* It is impossible to do enchanting when Dragon Aspect is active. If you attempt to enchant something, you receive the message, "Insufficient charge for enchantment".
*If you use this shout against [[Skyrim:Miraak (person)|Miraak]] at the summit of [[Skyrim:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]], he might say: "So, you use my own Shout against me. You learn quickly."
*If the Ancient Dragonborn appears, it will not replace any summons meaning it can be an additional third summon.

==Bugs==
{{Bug|The word walls in [[Skyrim:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]] and [[Skyrim:Raven Rock Mine|Raven Rock Mine]] may show two inscriptions on top of each other.|confirmed=1}}
**{{pc22}} Turning off collision with the console command <code>tcl</code> while approaching the word walls may solve this.
{{Bug|Sometimes if you are in a hold and you fall below 50% health with this shout still active, it will cause the Ancient Dragonborn to attack everyone in the hold.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|In rare cases, activating Dragon Aspect then immediately activating the Vampire Lord power can make the visual effect of Dragon Aspect permanent.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|In rare cases, activating Dragon Aspect can cause the sound effect to loop after the ability's timer runs out. To fix this reload the save prior to the effect ending.}}
